d Zone. Since no SOARecord has been added, getSOA() must still return null, proving that unrelated record types do not modify the SOA reference.'}]}, {'group': 'SOA retrieval - removal of unrelated records', 'cases': [{'input': [], 'expected': 'instance of the original SOARecord', 'description': 'Add a valid SOARecord and also add an unrelated ARecord. Remove the ARecord using removeRecord(Record). The SOARecord should remain untouched, so getSOA() must still return the original SOARecord.'}]}, {'group': 'SOA retrieval - zone cleared via iterator removal', 'cases': [{'input': [], 'expected': 'null', 'description': "Add an SOARecord to the Zone, obtain an iterator over the Zone's RRsets, and remove every RRset via the iterator's remove() method (or by calling removeRecord on each Record). After all records are removed, getSOA() should return null, confirming that the internal SOA reference is cleared when the zone becomes empty."}]}]
